  abstract={This article presents a fully integrated 4:1 dc-dc converter based on electromagnetically coupled Class-D LC (EMLC) oscillators. A series-transmission and parallel-reception (STPR) topology is proposed to achieve a scalable conversion ratio without significant efficiency degradation. Three power-transmitting oscillators (PTOs) and one merged power-receiving oscillator (PRO) are coupled at once via an on-chip quad-stacked transformer, resulting in a compact layout that reduces the required area and complexity. A prototype IC implemented in a 28-nm CMOS process achieves a high conversion ratio of 4:1 with a peak efficiency of 74.5% and supports input voltage up to 3.6 V. It achieves a peak power density of 0.78 W/mm2 while maintaining efficiency above 67% at peak power density. The converter also supports 1:4 step-up and 4:3 step-down conversions, delivering peak efficiencies of 74.3% and 90.3%, with peak power densities of 0.68 and 3.27 W/mm2, respectively.},
